{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "An Cư — selection-bound contract drafts",
    "version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "Implemented 14 October 2026. Private DRAFT authoring/review; no signing, activation, payment or release endpoints. Snapshots are server-derived and immutable. Monthly rent must be positive; all other money nonnegative. Existing legacy ACTIVE fixtures are not backfilled into these authoring routes. Legal identity/certificate fields are server-derived and frozen at creation; old snapshots remain unchanged and readable. Explicit local samples are marked; no eKYC or legal evidence proof. Update27October: new contexts prefer persisted VERIFIED Auth0 citizen; missing issue fields stay null, old snapshots unchanged. Context includes current rightsValidFrom/Until. Server locks/rechecks rights and rejects contract beyond approved window or expired rights."
  },
